  "code": "2000",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p>Ceruloplasmin is a copper oxide enzyme synthesized in liver playing a major role regulating the ionic state of iron and&nbsp;metallic ions in serum and at the cell surface. Decreased levels are seen in hepatolenticular degeneration or Wilson's&nbsp;disease and Menke's Kinky hair syndrome. Levels are elevated by the acute phase response and particularly by estrogens.The reagent in linear up to 100 mg/dl. Lower detection limit is 7 mg/dl</p>",
